The Pony grammar and queries come from tree-sitter-pony
(https://github.com/tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-pony), revision
73ff874ae4c9e9b45462673cbc0a1e350e2522a7:

- grammar.wasm is that revision's src/ built by scripts/build-grammar.sh (tree-sitter CLI 0.27.1).
- queries/highlights.scm, folds.scm, indents.scm and tags.scm are adapted from its queries/ for
  Orlo: `#lua-match?` became `#match?`, Neovim capture names became the ones Orlo maps
  (`@conditional` to `@keyword.conditional`, `@field` to `@property`, ...), the
  `#set! "priority"` pattern moved below the one it overrode, `@spell`/`@error` were dropped,
  indents.scm uses `@indent.begin`/`@indent.end`/`@indent.branch` and drops `@auto`, and
  tags.scm keeps only its definitions.

language.json and samples/ are Orlo's. tree-sitter-pony's license:

